# I18n

This player’s UI is Chinese while `Localization.GetCurrentLanguageCode()` is often `"en"`. Loading only `en.po` leaves mod text English.

- Keep English `LocString` msgid; put translations in `translations/{zh,ja,ko,ru}.po` with matching `msgctxt`.
- Hook `Localization.Initialize` Postfix → `CanisMinor.Shared.LocalePo.Register(...)`. Do not copy-paste LoadStringsFile into each mod.
- Shared loader: `src/Shared/LocalePo.cs` (via `src/Directory.Build.props`). Locale list includes `GetLocale().Code`, `GetCurrentLanguageCode()`, aliases (`schinese` → `zh`), `Application.systemLanguage`, and Hangul / kana / Cyrillic / CJK hints.
- Log folder, codes, and whether a `.po` loaded. `codes=en` + Chinese UI is a bug.
- `BuildingFacades.Add` / `PermitResource` snapshot strings. Resolve `STRINGS.*` at register time, after the `.po` load.
- AfterBuild must copy `translations/` into `local/<Mod>/translations/`.
